-- ============================================================================
-- D4 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Data-Driven Production Forecasting, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/forecastml/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: SMOOTHING A RATE SERIES INTO A FORECAST. A monthly rate
-- series and the one-step and h-step forecasts; simple exponential smoothing,
-- its level and alpha, the start at the first month and the flat forecast,
-- alpha at 1 as the naive forecast; Holt's linear trend, the second month
-- spent on the start and where scoring starts; the damped trend, phi, the
-- flattening and its limit; the parameter fit by the least one-step sum of
-- squared errors on a grid and a compass search, parameters on their bounds;
-- the NIST handbook as a published check. Digest sections 1 to 10, and
-- section 25.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A fit is in-sample: a low MSE says how well a
-- method followed months it had already seen, and a straight trend runs below
-- zero on a well that cannot. The Associate capstone grades six Associate
-- quantities and grades no backtest, no interval and no Arps baseline.
-- ============================================================================

values ('forecastml', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-data-driven-forecast-is","title":"What a Data-Driven Forecast Is","lesson_keys":["l01-a-rate-series-month-by-month","l02-forecasting-from-the-series-alone","l03-the-ekene-production-wells","l04-one-step-and-h-step-forecasts","l05-the-refusals-by-name"]},{"key":"m02-simple-exponential-smoothing","title":"Simple Exponential Smoothing","lesson_keys":["l01-the-level-and-alpha","l02-starting-at-the-first-month","l03-a-flat-forecast","l04-alpha-at-one-is-the-naive-forecast"]},{"key":"m03-holts-linear-trend","title":"Holt''s Linear Trend","lesson_keys":["l01-a-level-and-a-trend","l02-the-second-month-is-spent","l03-where-scoring-starts","l04-a-trend-that-runs-below-zero"]},{"key":"m04-the-damped-trend","title":"The Damped Trend","lesson_keys":["l01-damping-the-trend-with-phi","l02-the-damped-forecast-flattens","l03-the-limit-of-a-damped-forecast","l04-phi-fitted-and-phi-given","l05-damped-with-phi-at-one-is-holt"]},{"key":"m05-fitting-the-parameters","title":"Fitting the Parameters","lesson_keys":["l01-the-sum-of-squared-errors","l02-the-grid-then-the-compass-search","l03-parameters-on-their-bounds","l04-convergence-and-the-stop-rule"]},{"key":"m06-one-well-forecast","title":"One Well Forecast, End to End","lesson_keys":["l01-the-whole-workflow","l02-the-nist-handbook-as-a-check","l03-writing-up-a-forecast","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
